# Ticket Domain Rules

## Status transitions (enforced in TicketsService)

| Action | Endpoint | Allowed from | Actor |
|--------|----------|--------------|-------|
| Submit | `PATCH /tickets/:id/submit` | DRAFT | Creator |
| Approve/Reject/Info | `PATCH /tickets/:id/approve` | NEW, AWAITING_APPROVAL | PROGRAMMING_HEAD |
| Assign | `PATCH /tickets/:id/assign` | APPROVED | MANAGER, HEAD |
| Start | `PATCH /tickets/:id/start` | SCHEDULED, APPROVED | DEVELOPER |
| Submit for testing | `PATCH /tickets/:id/submit-for-testing` | IN_PROGRESS | DEVELOPER |
| Verify testing | `PATCH /tickets/:id/approve-completion` | AWAITING_TESTING | QA, MANAGER, HEAD |
| Accept delivery | `PATCH /tickets/:id/approve-completion` | AWAITING_OWNER_APPROVAL | Creator, SYSTEM_OWNER (in scope), MANAGER, HEAD |
| Close | `PATCH /tickets/:id/close` | COMPLETED | MANAGER, HEAD |

## Approval decisions

`APPROVED` · `REJECTED` · `NEEDS_INFO` · `CONVERT_TO_PROJECT`

## Visibility rules

- `TICKET_REQUESTER`: own tickets only
- `DEVELOPER`: assigned + mentioned + system/company access
- `SYSTEM_OWNER`: company tickets
- `PROGRAMMING_HEAD` / `PROJECT_MANAGER`: all tickets

## Comments

- `PUBLIC` — visible to requester
- `INTERNAL` — programming team only

## Never

- Skip approval before IN_PROGRESS
- Close without closure notes
- Expose internal comments to requesters
